From 3d739476c93bc602d3bc179f7fcc8c43d86e2c76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:43:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(animation): animate floating-window minimize and
 restore

A minimized floating window used to disappear in one frame. It now fades and
collapses toward a configurable anchor under `[animation.windows_minimize]`,
and the restore plays the same timeline in reverse from the collapsed box.

The live view is animated instead of a snapshot: minimize keeps the surface,
box and stacking slot, so hiding it is presentation, not unmap. The node stays
enabled through the fade and the enable gate relaxes only while a conceal is
in flight; `animateTo` refuses layout retargets meanwhile, and the fade binds
no lifecycle shader because minimize has no effect slot.

State reporting, focus handoff and taskbars stay immediate.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
