From 225b2401859d4e8620c9c7ea2b47cd126cb1f3da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:15:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(animation): keep the minimize fade out of the
 lifecycle shader

Review fixes for the minimize animation:

- The reveal re-enabled the lifecycle fade, so it ran the opening program and
  the border and title bar snapped to full opacity while the client was
  shader-faded. Both directions of a minimize fade now suppress it, and the
  state is derived from the two directions instead of a third flag.
- A restore that will not animate could leave a conceal running, whose finish
  then hid a window that was no longer minimized. Abandoning the transition
  restores the resting box and cancels the tweens, and the finish itself
  delegates there when the window was restored meanwhile. Maximize,
  fullscreen and a new placement abandon it too, since they re-place the
  window in a state it has to be seen in.
- windows_in.style = "slide" no longer warps the minimize opacity with sqrt.

The harness now proves the reveal is the conceal reversed, that a windows_in
program never runs on either direction, that a slide style does not brighten
the fade, and that unminimizing mid-conceal leaves the window drawn.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
