From 69747b4fc987fd8d27e3b25aefe62897818d12d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:27:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(animation): keep a mid-conceal restore on its resting
 box

A conceal retargets the live node to its collapsed origin, so a restore
that arrived mid-conceal read that origin as its resting box and finished
off-centre and small. The reveal now starts from the box captured when the
conceal began, reverses from what is actually drawn, and an unmap mid-fade
restores the resting box instead of waiting for a presentation.

The fade keeps the node enabled, so a click on the fading remnant used to
focus and unminimize it; hit-testing now skips a concealing view. The
minimize state is one phase enum rather than two bools, and the
`bottom_center` anchor rests the scaled box's bottom edge on the usable
bottom instead of centring it half outside.

The harness gains the missing animated restore-mid-conceal leg with bbox
assertions and a click-during-conceal leg.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
