From a701c0de0d0b9af26125dea322a5dbaa682f2a2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:49:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(animation): refuse input on a fading window's
 decorated frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The content hit test already skipped a concealing view, but the SSD
frame tree did not, so a press on the fading title bar focused the view —
and focusing a minimized view restores it. The same guard now covers
`ssdFrameAt`, so the border cannot start a resize and the close button
cannot fire either.

A reveal that interrupts a conceal also retargets the box even when the
style was reloaded to `fade` mid-flight, because the conceal is what moved
it. A `windows_move` preset no longer warps the collapse, which is meant
to be geometry and plain alpha only.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
